# Caddy snippet for stock-mcp.
#
# Mirrors the ipmcp.kitepon.dynv6.net block in /home/kite/license-server/Caddyfile.
# Why a dedicated subdomain (not a path under kitepon.dynv6.net):
#   the kitepon.dynv6.net root server block in the same Caddyfile has a
#   catch-all `reverse_proxy * api:3000`, so path-based MCP routes would be
#   swallowed by ConnectC2X / license-server. Each MCP gets its own subdomain.
#
# Apply:
#   1. Append this block to /home/kite/license-server/Caddyfile
#   2. docker exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   3. Verify: curl -I https://stockmcp.kitepon.dynv6.net/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
#
# Requires:
#   - DNS A record for stockmcp.kitepon.dynv6.net pointing to the home IP
#   - Caddy's automatic ACME / Let's Encrypt is already operating for the
#     other subdomains in this Caddyfile (no extra config needed).
#   - stock-mcp.service running on 192.168.1.2:39200 with OAuth env vars set
#   - STOCK_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS / STOCK_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS include
#     stockmcp.kitepon.dynv6.net (FastMCP DNS-rebinding guard).

stockmcp.kitepon.dynv6.net {
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		-X-Powered-By
		-Server
	}
	reverse_proxy 192.168.1.2:39200 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
